            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0366" n="254" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 818.00/384</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-05T10:00:00-05:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 5, 1918, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Constitutional guaranties suspended by Congress at dictation of Executive for 30
                    days, in view of “threatened foreign invasion.” Have received no news from
                    American Legation Panama as to the basis for reported movement from there.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
